WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.534
-Hey, what's up, Jim?
What's going on, buddy?

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.837
-It's so good to see you.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.373
Man, it has been a while
since the first time I told you

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:11.911
the first I saw you was at my
high school in Saugerties.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.846
-Yeah, that's pretty awesome,
Saugerties.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.848
-Yeah, it was like
a Golden Glove

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:17.283
or something like that.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.818
-I don't know.
Probably was just a local

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.720
amateur fight or something.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.290
-Yeah, and I remember our
local shoe store, Montano's,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.760
sold you a pair of boxing shoes
or something like that,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.628
and I was like --
I love that you got --

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:31.330
like, that was a big legend
around my hometown growing up

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:34.433
was that, "Mike Tyson got his
boxing shoes from Montano's!"

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:35.668
It was the coolest thing ever.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.104
And now, here you are,
Mike Tyson is back.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.341
Iron Mike. September 12th.
-Oh, man, I'm so happy.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.842
Yeah, man.
It's gonna be so awesome.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.845
I'm so happy
to be coming back into the ring

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.546
and facing Roy Jones
on September 12th.

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:48.982
It's gonna be so awesome.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:52.284
And by doing that, I'm also --
Jimmy, I'm gonna be launching --

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:53.920
Being the prototype of it,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.156
I'm launching
my Legends Only League.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.856
And this is gonna be so awesome.

00:00:57.856 --> 00:01:00.927
Other leagues from all over --
whoever, I don't care.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:04.864
Basketball, pool shark,
all the ex-legends

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.433
who want to play
and still able to play

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.502
and still beautiful,
like myself,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.371
they can come with us,
they can call me.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.840
We can have anybody.
Like, before, I was saying,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:19.279
we have Dennis Rodman go against
Metta World Peace, one on one,

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.848
have Wayne Gretzky go against
an up-and-coming young guy,

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:25.151
one on one,
have their team together.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.787
Everybody.
-That's a great idea.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.155
But this is, like --

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:32.525
How'd it come about,
first fight in 15 years?

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:35.461
How did it happen?
Why?

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.563
-Well, I don't know.
I wanted to do something good.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:42.301
I'm embarked
on a real charitable event,

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:45.538
and oh, man, we're gonna help
so many various charities.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.273
And I thought
it was a great thing to do.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.375
And, of course,
I can still do it, of course.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.211
So, this is what I want to do.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.479
I'm really
looking forward to it.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:58.317
-And did you pick Roy Jones Jr.
out of a lineup?

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:01.354
'Cause you could fight anyone.
-Hey, I don't know.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:04.390
It's a whole bunch of guys.
It started out with Bob Sapp,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.193
and I got from Bob Sapp
to Roy Jones.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.862
I don't know how this happened,
but I think he's brilliant,

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.931
'cause he's the greatest fighter
of his generation.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.800
I'm the greatest fighter
of my generation,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.637
and it's just a no-brainer that
we should clash together.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.672
-Yeah. You guys
never fought before, right?

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.775
-No, we planned on fighting,
but it didn't happen,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.977
but this is the opportunity now.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.980
-I saw the training footage
of you on Instagram,

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.483
and, oh, my gosh!
You've got it, man.

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:33.953
It's unbelievable.
-I'm back, man, I'm back.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.122
I don't know how come
it came back.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:39.792
I started training.
I'm back in shape. I'm 228.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.927
And I've been boxing.
Doing what I can.

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:43.295
I can't believe
this either, man.

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:45.764
It's just -- I don't believe
in the Fountain of Youth,

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:48.501
but something just came over me,
and I'm back, man.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:54.574
-How does it feel training from
54 compared to when you were 24?

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.577
-Well, it's really painful.
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:00.846
-Really painful.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:02.915
And from
this experience right now,

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:04.717
I'll never call
another fighter a bum again,

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.352
because anybody that does this

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.720
or attempts to do this
is no bum.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.556
-Yeah, it's tough.
It's rough.

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:13.025
How do your kids
feel about you coming back?

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.161
-Well, my kids think
I should sit my old ass down,

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:18.030
but what do they know?
Of course. You know?

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.532
I'm very confident.
They don't know how to fight.

00:03:20.532 --> 00:03:22.568
Neither one of my kids
can beat me in a fight,

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.370
so what are they talking about?
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.005
What are they talking about?
Yeah. Come on.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.674
-Wait till they see
what dad does.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.609
-Absolutely.
-I have a prediction.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:33.913
-I think -- well, I know you're
gonna win because I know you.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.714
You're Mike Tyson.
I think --

00:03:35.714 --> 00:03:37.850
How long is a round?
Three minutes?

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.718
-Three minutes.
Three minutes.

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:41.888
-I think, here's what happens.
I think, in your head,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.457
you're gonna
want to go five rounds.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.526
But I think once you get in
there and that thing

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:52.298
and you get tagged once,
the hurricane's gonna come out,

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.632
the Iron Mike
is gonna come out,

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:59.004
and you're gonna lose it.
I'm gonna say...fourth round.

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:00.639
And that's being nice.

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:03.575
-Well, why don't we just
do a lottery and find out.

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:05.811
-Yeah. Oh, definitely.

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:09.014
I'll fly to you.
-Absolutely.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:11.884
This is gonna be so awesome.
This is gonna be so awesome.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.787
-"Iron Mike" --
did that come from Cus D'Amato?

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.255
Where'd you get the nickname
"Iron Mike"?

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:19.292
-Somebody just started
calling me "Iron Mike,"

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:23.329
a gentleman that hung out with a
friend of mine, Carlos Santos.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.831
And he had said,
"Man, I'll buy you a T-shirt

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:27.799
that says 'Iron Mike.'
I didn't even know what

00:04:27.799 --> 00:04:30.937
that stands for, and now
everybody calls me "Iron Mike."

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.972
-Wow.
See, I didn't know that.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:36.609
And then I just saw
some pictures of Jamie Foxx,

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.077
who is unbelievable.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.546
I love that guy.
He's so talented.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.815
He's playing you in a movie
called "Finding Mike."

00:04:43.815 --> 00:04:45.117
It's finally happened.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.553
We talked about it last time
you were on the show.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.790
And so now
it's finally happening.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.692
-Hey, man,
I'm looking forward to this.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:56.028
This is gonna be really
interesting, observing myself.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:05:00.266
-Yeah. But Jamie said to me
when he was here last time,

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.134
we're talking in the hallway,
and he said,

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:04.970
"I got tons of Mike stories.
Like, we hung out.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.506
I've been through everything."
Like, he was with you

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:09.842
through the good times
and the bad times.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.278
-Jamie might also
be participating

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.514
in the Legends Only League,
as well, because I'm sure

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.749
there's some comedians
that want to kick his ass.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.017
-[ Laughing ]
-So we can get Jamie

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.687
to participate
in this stuff, as well.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:23.522
Listen, it's for all athletes.
I'm talking about anybody --

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:26.292
ping pong players,
all legendary handball players,

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.294
all the legends of the past,

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:31.697
you know,
who's around 45, 50 years old.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:34.433
Come with me.
Tell your agents to call me.

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.502
Get in shape.
I'm talking about anybody.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.472
I don't care who you are.
Everybody.

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.140
We can always
have something for you.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.507
Legends don't have to stand out.

00:05:42.507 --> 00:05:44.410
Of course, if they're still
beautiful, like myself,

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.412
and still able to do
what they do,

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.081
so why do they have to
not do what they do?

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:51.049
You can still have
a great football team,

00:05:51.049 --> 00:05:53.585
basketball team,
one-on-one tennis,

00:05:53.585 --> 00:05:56.622
one-on-one ping pong, whatever,
handball, whatever.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.925
Basketball, football.
Whatever it is, we got it.

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:01.660
-Yeah, just because
you got older,

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.664
doesn't mean
you're not still an athlete.

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:07.300
-Exactly!
How many people you know

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.002
can still outrun Jerry Rice,
really?

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.171
-No. No one.
-Exactly.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.939
-No one I know.
-Exactly.

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:15.741
And I bet you --
And I bet you he has

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:18.811
more fan bases
and more YouTube followers

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.580
than the guy that plays
his position

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.214
in the team he used to play for.

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:24.750
-Yeah. Yeah,
I think it's a great idea.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.285
-Exactly.
He doesn't have to die.

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:29.187
Why does he have to die because
they say he can't play no more?

00:06:29.187 --> 00:06:31.657
-[ Laughing ] Exactly.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:34.059
I'm so excited about this.
September 12th.

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:36.595
And if anyone needs
any more reason be to excited

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:39.698
for the fight,
take a look at this.

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:42.101
-Why do I want to be
the baddest man on the planet?

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:44.170
Sometimes I wish I could stop
having these desires

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.371
to go forward,
to think that I'm somebody,

00:06:46.371 --> 00:06:48.407
'cause it's a lot of work.

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:52.210
-You got to be willing
to get up every morning, 5:00,

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.113
hit that rope, every day.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:56.015
Certain time, hit that gym.

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:59.018
Because that other man over
there is willing to do anything

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.920
that he got to do necessary
to win.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.888
-Human beings are not
meant to be humble.

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:04.990
-Nobody ever went
from junior middleweight

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.092
and became heavyweight champ.
I took off and did it.

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:10.095
-We're not born to be humble.
We born to be humbled.

00:07:10.095 --> 00:07:13.266
-It's like David and Goliath.
He's this monster we know.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:15.434
If he hits you,
he can take your head off,

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:19.304
and I'm little old David
who only has God on my side.

00:07:19.304 --> 00:07:22.107
-Tell me
who you want me to kill.

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:23.509
-That's what I'm talkin' about.

